<TextPage title="Fastest uncensored AI models: latency and throughput compared" description="Which uncensored AI models deliver the fastest responses? Benchmarked time-to-first-token, tokens per second, and end-to-end latency." kicker="Feature comparison" noindex={true}>
  <div class="empty-state"><strong>Live benchmark pending.</strong><p>Speed scores publish after all models complete the same benchmark version. This page remains noindex until then.</p></div>
  <h2>Speed matters more than most reviews admit</h2>
  <p>In roleplay, a 4-second delay between exchanges breaks flow. In chat, a model that streams 3 tokens per second feels sluggish; one at 40 tokens per second feels responsive. Speed is not a vanity metric — it directly affects whether users stick with a platform or abandon it.</p>
  <h2>What we measure</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Time to first token (TTFT):</strong> How long before the first word appears? Under 500ms is ideal; over 2 seconds is noticeable.</li>
    <li><strong>Tokens per second (TPS):</strong> The streaming throughput once generation begins. Reading speed is ~10–15 TPS; anything above 20 TPS feels instant.</li>
    <li><strong>End-to-end latency:</strong> Total wall-clock time from request to last token, including network round-trip and any provider-side queuing.</li>
    <li><strong>Error and retry rate:</strong> How often does the provider return a 429 (rate limit), 503 (overloaded), or timeout?</li>
  </ul>
  <p>All measurements use the same fixed prompt length and max-token setting so comparisons are like-for-like.</p>
  <h2>What affects speed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Model size:</strong> A 12B model can run 3–5× faster than a 405B model on equivalent hardware.</li>
    <li><strong>Provider routing:</strong> OpenRouter routes to different upstream providers; speed can vary by route even for the same model ID.</li>
    <li><strong>Time of day:</strong> Shared-provider latency spikes during peak hours. We test at multiple times and report the range.</li>
    <li><strong>Streaming vs. batch:</strong> Streaming reduces perceived latency (TTFT is faster) but can increase total wall-clock time.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Speed leaders (architecture-based estimate)</h2>
  <p>Small models on dedicated providers (UnslopNemo 12B, Dolphin Mistral 24B) are expected to lead on throughput. Venice's native API routes avoid OpenRouter's intermediary hop and may offer lower TTFT. Large models (Hermes 3 405B) will be slower but may justify the wait with higher-quality output. Live results will confirm.</p>
